{
  // sui-eval-smoke — haiku-only single-lane variant of `sui-eval` for cheap
  // end-to-end validation of the harness (daemon fanout → grade → record),
  // especially after the #193 watcher-leak fix unblocked the daemon path.
  // Live graded A/B runs use `sui-eval` (haiku + sonnet). Test runs use THIS.
  "name": "sui-eval-smoke",
  "description": "SUI authoring eval — single haiku lane, smoke-test the grade/record chain.",
  "auto_merge": false,
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "build",
      "agent": "ship-designer",
      "fanout": {
        "lanes": [
          { "id": "haiku", "agent": "ship-designer", "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001" }
        ],
        "judge": { "step": "grade" },
        "min_successful_lanes": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "grade",
      "after": ["build"],
      "run": "bun .ship/pipelines/sui-eval/scripts/grade.ts\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "record",
      "after": ["grade"],
      "run": "bun .ship/pipelines/sui-eval/scripts/record.ts\n"
    }
  ],
  "step_specs": [
    "SMOKE TASK (intentionally tiny — this validates the harness/fanout plumbing, not authoring quality; do NOT gold-plate). Create `views/smoke-counter/`: page.sui (an <h1>, a count read from a signal, and a + button with on:click that increments it), controller.ts (scope: { count: signal(0) }), and manifest.jsonc ({ name, path: \"/smoke-counter\", title, layout: \"default\", auth: \"public\" }). Keep it under ~40 lines total. Verify it compiles: `cargo run -q -p sui-compiler -- build views/smoke-counter/page.sui --component-name smoke-counter --out /tmp/smoke`. Then call `ship ops call pipelines.step_done --json '{\"slug\":\"'\"'$SHIP_ACTOR_ID'\"'\",\"summary\":\"smoke-counter built + compiles\"}'`. Stop there.\n",
    "",
    ""
  ]
}
